@startuml sequence_diagram_role_change_enforcement
autonumber
skinparam shadowing true
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true

title Sequence Diagram - WEB03 Role or Account-Status Change while the SPA is Open (back-end enforcement, non-recursive 401/403 handling)

actor User as "Manager\n(SPA open on /manage/stock)"
actor Admin as "Administrator\n(AA06)"
participant Page as "StockPage\n(WEB05)"
participant API as "apiClient\n(WEB01, extended)"
participant Auth as "AuthProvider"
participant Menu as "NavigationMenu"
participant Guard as "ProtectedRoute"
participant AuthMW as "AuthMiddleware"
participant RoleMW as "RoleMiddleware"
participant Service as "UserService"
database DB as "Database\n(Persistence)"

note over User, DB
    The menu shown to the user was built when the roles were last confirmed (SD 1 / SD 2).
    A change made in the meantime is enforced by the BACK END on the very next protected
    request (AA03: resolveActor reloads the User every time), so no further protected
    operation is accepted with the withdrawn permissions (AC 6).
    Handling rule (3.4, BR 13): only BUSINESS requests reach handleAuthFailure();
    401 is terminal (no /auth/me); 403 causes at most ONE /auth/me (single-flight);
    /auth/me is sent with skipAuthFailureHandler = true, so its answer never re-enters the handler.
end note

Admin -> DB : removes MANAGER from the user (AA06)\nroles: [CUSTOMER, MANAGER] -> [CUSTOMER]\n(or: deactivates the account / the token expires)
note right of Admin : no new login is required for\nthe change to take effect

User -> Page : submits "Adjust stock" (button visible: menu is stale)
activate Page
Page -> API : request("POST", "/stock/{productId}/adjustments", { body })
activate API
API -> AuthMW : POST ... Authorization: Bearer <token>
activate AuthMW
AuthMW -> Service : resolveActor(token)
activate Service
Service -> DB : SELECT ... FROM users WHERE id = $1
activate DB
DB --> Service : row (current roles, active)
deactivate DB

alt A) Token expired / invalid or user deleted
    Service --> AuthMW : throw AppError("Invalid or expired token", 401)
    AuthMW --> API : 401 { error: { message: "Invalid or expired token", status: 401 } }
else B) Account deactivated (or left with no role)
    Service -> Service : assertCanAccess(user)
    Service --> AuthMW : throw AppError("Account is not active", 403)
    AuthMW --> API : 403 { error: { message: "Account is not active", status: 403 } }
    note right of AuthMW : RoleMiddleware and controller NOT executed:\nstock is not changed
else C) Active, roles = [CUSTOMER]
    Service -> Service : assertCanAccess(user)
    Service --> AuthMW : AuthenticatedActor { roles: ["CUSTOMER"] }
    AuthMW -> RoleMW : next()
    activate RoleMW
    RoleMW -> RoleMW : requireRole("MANAGER")\n["CUSTOMER"] has none of [MANAGER]
    RoleMW --> API : 403 { error: { message: "Forbidden: insufficient permissions", status: 403 } }
    deactivate RoleMW
    note right of RoleMW : controller NOT executed:\nstock is not changed
end
deactivate Service
deactivate AuthMW

== The SPA reacts BEFORE the error is returned to the page (business request -> handler invoked) ==

API -> Auth : handleAuthFailure(status)
activate Auth

alt status = 401 (branch A) - TERMINAL
    Auth -> Auth : clear(): discard token (AA04);\nstatus = "guest"
    Auth -> Guard : state changed
    activate Guard
    Guard -> Guard : evaluateAccess(stock, auth) = LOGIN_REQUIRED
    Guard -> Page : unmount
    Guard --> User : redirect to /login?returnTo=/manage/stock
    deactivate Guard
    note right of Auth
        NO refresh(), NO /auth/me request,
        NO retry of the business request.
        The flow ends here.
    end note

else status = 403 (branches B and C)
    alt status is already "guest" / "denied" (no token)
        Auth -> Auth : no-op (nothing to clear or refresh)
    else authenticated
        Auth -> Auth : refresh()\nsingle-flight: if a refresh is in progress,\nreturn the SAME promise (no new request)
        Auth -> API : authApi.getCurrentUser()\nrequest("GET", "/auth/me", { skipAuthFailureHandler: true })
        API -> AuthMW : GET /api/v1/auth/me (Bearer)
        activate AuthMW
        AuthMW --> API : 200 { roles } / 401 / 403 / 5xx
        deactivate AuthMW
        note right of API
            skipAuthFailureHandler = true:
            the apiClient does NOT call handleAuthFailure()
            for this answer; it only resolves / rejects.
            => an /auth/me answer can never start
            another /auth/me request (no recursion).
        end note
        API --> Auth : result (mapped by table A, 3.4)

        alt A') /auth/me -> 401
            Auth -> Auth : clear(); status = "guest"\n(flow ends, login on protected section)
        else B') /auth/me -> 403 "Account is not active"
            Auth -> Auth : clear(); status = "denied";\ndeniedMessage = message (flow ends)
        else C') /auth/me -> 200 { roles: ["CUSTOMER"] }
            Auth -> Auth : currentUser.roles = ["CUSTOMER"]
        else D') /auth/me -> 200 with the SAME roles
            Auth -> Auth : nothing changed: the operation itself\nwas not permitted for this user
        else E') /auth/me -> 5xx / network / malformed
            Auth -> Auth : clear(); status = "guest" (fail closed)
        end

        Auth -> Menu : state changed
        activate Menu
        Menu -> Menu : getVisibleSections(auth)
        Menu --> User : menu rebuilt (A', B', E': public only;\nC': restaurant management, kitchen\nand planning groups removed; D': unchanged)
        deactivate Menu

        Auth -> Guard : state changed
        activate Guard
        Guard -> Guard : evaluateAccess(stock, auth)
        alt decision is no longer ALLOW (A', B', C', E')
            Guard -> Page : unmount (stock data removed from the screen)
            Guard --> User : LoginPage / AccessDeniedPage (ACCOUNT_DENIED message /\n"You do not have permission to access this page.")
        else D') still ALLOW
            Guard -> Guard : keep the page
        end
        deactivate Guard
    end
end
deactivate Auth

API --> Page : rejects with ApiError(401 | 403)\n(business request is NOT retried)
deactivate API
Page --> User : (only if still mounted, D') error feedback (WEB04):\n"You do not have permission to perform this operation."\noperation NOT shown as completed, input preserved
deactivate Page

note over User, DB
    The same back-end checks (AuthMiddleware -> RoleMiddleware) apply when the request does not come
    from the SPA at all (e.g. curl with a valid token), so hiding the menu option is never the only
    protection (AC 7, AA05).
end note

@enduml